From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden PS4 <eden-ps4@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:52:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: shader draws in software

The null rasterizer's draws go to a software renderer: the vertex and
fragment programs are translated by the shader recompiler and their IR
flattened (phis as moves on each edge of the structured control flow)
into operations on numbered cells, which an interpreter runs. Vertices
are fetched from the vertex streams (float, unorm, snorm, int, scaled;
indexed or not, instanced), shaded, clipped against w > 0, mapped to the
window as the Vulkan renderer maps them, culled, and rasterized into
render target 0 in emulated memory a block at a time, with varyings
interpolated as Vulkan would (perspective, linear, flat) and blending.
Not done yet: textures, depth and stencil, more than one render target,
points and lines; draws that need them are skipped and logged once.
